# The finite power sums, the polynomial shadows of the Riemann zeta function. The zeta function packages the infinite
# sums of reciprocal powers, and its values at the even arguments are rational multiples of powers of pi set by the
# Bernoulli numbers, the same Bernoulli numbers that appear as the constant terms of the Eisenstein series the lattice
# theta functions belong to. The finite cousins, the sums of the first n k-th powers, have exact closed forms, the
# Faulhaber family, and this file DEFINES those sums by recurrence and PROVES their closed forms for every n by induction,
# so the statements are laws over all naturals, not checks at sample points. The cube sum is the one that matters most
# here: its closed form is Nicomachus's theorem, the sum of the first n cubes is the SQUARE of the sum of the first n
# numbers, and the cubes are exactly what the eight-dimensional theta series counts, two hundred forty times the cube
# divisor sums. The base case and the inductive step are both discharged by the commutative-ring normalizer, no value is
# ever computed, so each proof certifies the identity as a polynomial identity over the integers.

# The sum of the first n natural numbers, by the recurrence sum(n) = sum(n-1) + n with sum(0) = 0.
task sum
  take n, like natural-number
  like natural-number
  send back
    fork test
      hook test
        call is-equal
          read n
          code 0
      hook hold
        code 0
      hook miss
        call add
          call sum
            call subtract
              read n
              code 1
          read n

# The sum of the first n cubes, by the recurrence cube-sum(n) = cube-sum(n-1) + n^3 with cube-sum(0) = 0.
task cube-sum
  take n, like natural-number
  like natural-number
  send back
    fork test
      hook test
        call is-equal
          read n
          code 0
      hook hold
        code 0
      hook miss
        call add
          call cube-sum
            call subtract
              read n
              code 1
          call multiply
            read n
            call multiply
              read n
              read n

# Gauss's triangular closed form, proved first because Nicomachus is stated against it: twice the sum of the first n
# numbers is n times n plus one, 2 * sum(n) = n * (n + 1), for every n. So the sum of the first n numbers is the n-th
# triangular number.
rule twice-the-sum-is-n-times-n-plus-one
  seat n, like natural-number
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        code 2
        call sum
          read n
      call multiply
        read n
        call add
          read n
          code 1
  fold n

# NICOMACHUS'S THEOREM: the sum of the first n cubes is the SQUARE of the sum of the first n numbers, so with denominators
# cleared, four times the sum of the first n cubes is the square of n times n plus one, 4 * cube-sum(n) = (n * (n + 1))^2,
# for every n. Combined with the triangular form above, this says cube-sum(n) equals sum(n) squared: the sum of cubes is
# the square of the triangular number. It is the finite power-sum identity at the cube, the shadow of zeta at the third
# power, and the cubes it governs are exactly what the eight-dimensional theta series counts.
rule four-times-sum-of-cubes-is-n-times-n-plus-one-squared
  seat n, like natural-number
  show hold
    call is-equal
      call multiply
        code 4
        call cube-sum
          read n
      call multiply
        call multiply
          read n
          call add
            read n
            code 1
        call multiply
          read n
          call add
            read n
            code 1
  fold n
